# /etc/disk-guard.env — config for disk-guard.sh (0600 root)
#
# Create a "Push" monitor in Uptime Kuma (uptime.owner.example) named
# "agent-box disk" (or "ops-1 disk") and paste its push URL here.
#
# THE INTERVAL RULE (ORB-154, do not skip this). The monitor's heartbeat interval
# AND its retry interval must both be at least TWICE disk-guard.timer's period.
# The timer runs every 10 minutes, so both are 1500s. This monitor was originally
# created with a 600s window against that same ~610s pusher, and the result was a
# one-second race: Kuma declared "No heartbeat in the time window" a moment before
# each push landed, then went green a second later, forever. 111 false downs, every
# one of them a Slack message. Details in docs/runbooks/box-alerting.md.
KUMA_PUSH_URL=

# Optional overrides (defaults shown):
# THRESHOLD=75
# MOUNT=/
